// Auto-generated from a stock silhouette-dancer clip (user-provided MP4,
// 8.0s-10.4s, a clean solo-dancing window -- an earlier/later segment of the
// same clip briefly includes a second dancer's hand reaching into frame,
// which is why this particular range was picked). Crop bounds were measured
// pixel-exactly in Python across every frame of the segment (min/max extent
// of above-threshold content), then padded by a fixed *proportion* of that
// measured height (15% top, 3% bottom, 5% each side) before scaling to a
// height shared by all four dancerN_frames.h files -- proportional padding
// + a common target height is what makes the four look the same size and
// stand at the same floor line despite each source clip framing its dancer
// differently; padding by a fixed pixel amount per clip (the previous
// approach) did not. Thresholded to a 1-bit mask, packed row-by-row with
// each row padded to a byte boundary (matches blitDancer()'s read stride in
// main.cpp -- packing as one continuous bitstream instead desyncs it and
// shows up as diagonal shearing). Not a native loop -- played ping-pong
// (forward then backward) by the full-screen dancer visualizer, since
// ping-pong is seamless regardless of source content.
